<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-NOON RADIO HEADLINES - MARCH 27.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-NOON RADIO HEADLINES - MARCH 27.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the headlines on Estonian Kuku radio at noon. Reuters has not verified these reports and does not vouch for their accuracy:</p>
<p>-Washington-based Carnegie Foundation has invited former PM Mart Laar to become a member of its economic reform chamber.</p>
<p>-The most watched television programme in Estonia in February is &quot;Dating Game&quot; with one third of the population watching the show, and the average person watched four hours and 18 minutes of television a week.</p>
<p>- Parliament gave the corruption investigation committee increased investigative powers.</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
